# Ledger 0020: each block parameter's incoming arguments, listed once (blocks.awk, then ws64.awk).
# Entered from `_aliases`' B42 (the end of the first-appearance pass) with its 17 values; leaves for B52 (the first
# round's test) with word 9 = S and word 10 = A, two words the rounds carry but never read.
#   n = G_VCOUNT; S and W are n + 2 words each, A is S[n + 1] + 1 words, all from the arena (H_ARENA, H_ARENA_END).
#   Pass 1: for every block (G_BLIST order), edge and argument a, S[p + 1] += 1 for p = the target's parameter a.
#   S[i] += S[i - 1] for i = 1 .. n + 1; W = S.
#   Pass 2, in the same order: A[W[p]] = the argument; W[p] += 1.  So A[S[v] .. S[v + 1]) are the values every edge
#   passes to parameter v, in the order the rounds' scan of every edge met them.
# An exhausted arena gives NONE, as `_aliases`' own allocation does.

# b0: S and W.  Words 17.. of b1: S, W, n, i, 2(n + 2).
@H 0 0
n0.0 constant 29360173 -> T5
@LD n0.1 n0.0 p0.3 p0.5
n0.2 constant 2 -> T5
n0.3 add.wrap n0.1 n0.2 -> T5
n0.4 add.wrap n0.3 n0.3 -> T5
n0.5 constant 268435404 -> T5
@LD n0.6 n0.5 p0.3 n0.1.R1
n0.7 add.wrap n0.6 n0.4 -> T5
@ST n0.8 n0.5 p0.3 n0.7 n0.6.R1
n0.9 constant 268435405 -> T5
@LD n0.10 n0.9 p0.3 n0.8
n0.11 int.compare n0.7 n0.10 -> T6 [4]
n0.12 add.wrap n0.6 n0.3 -> T5
n0.13 constant 0 -> T5
cbr n0.11 b1({V 0},n0.10.R1,{S 0},n0.6,n0.12,n0.1,n0.13,n0.4) b99({V 0},n0.10.R1)

